(This analysis covers Naspers Limited \(NPN.JO\) daily returns. Normality is rejected at the 5% level \(Jarque-Bera p < 0.0001\).) Tj
T* (Returns are positively skewed and fat-tailed \(skew 0.38, excess kurtosis 8.49\), so large moves are more frequent than a normal) Tj
T* (model implies. At the 99% level, historical VaR is 6.47% versus 5.83% under a normal fit, so the normal model understates the) Tj
T* (daily tail loss by 1.1x. 13 days fell more than three standard deviations below the mean, versus about 3.0 expected under) Tj
T* (normality. The worst day was -17.70% and maximum drawdown was -62.8%. A Student-t fit with 3.9 degrees of freedom beats the) Tj
T* (normal fit by AIC 387. This describes the selected historical sample, not a forecast.) Tj
